t me saying  that you are required to like  those eras the moffett era the chimneal  era or that you have to like every  episode or every decision  creative that those people made you  don't  i'm just saying the people who are being  the harshest  who are calling for the harshest things  who are saying the  cruelest most  indefensible things at  the people responsible for the show they  have gotten  louder i don't honestly think there's  more of them than there used to be  but they have gotten louder and they've  gotten organized  which amplifies those voices more and i  would not blame  any creator even if they love doctor who  even if they  think they've got a great idea for  doctor who i would not blame any creator  who looks at this nonsense and not even  just with doctor who who looks at stuff  like what happened with the new star  wars trilogy who looks at  all the vitriol thrown at the creators  at the actors and at multiple of them  like people love to crap on ryan johnson  but then  rise of skywalker came out and nobody  liked that and now jj abrams is a huge  villain too whereas before he was seen  as  the good guy who made a good movie that  john's the script like  this vitriol knows no bounds and it can  and will hit  anybody i don't blame anyone who looks  at that and goes  no no i i don't  uh i don't want to deal with that  especially knowing that  certain stripes of fandom are going to  call them  cowards who don't listen to fans because  they don't address  bad faith arguments  it would not be an easy job in a vacuum  where social media doesn't exist  but social media does exist and it is  weaponized  these days by certain elements of fandom  and that is not something that you could  just pretend doesn't exist  it may impact some people some creators  some writers actors etc  harsher than others either depending on  that own person's ability to  cope or how much crap gets piled onto  them because i'm sorry  everyone has their limits  and it would be hard to look at what's  gone on with doctor who and doctor who  fandom and not go  me taking up this job is gonna put a  target on my  back and i don't really want it  so all this  being taken into account all of these  possible factors or possible  reasons should we be worried  about the fact that we don't have a new  showrunner announced  not yet but i would say  every week that goes by that we don't  have an announcement of a new showrunner  that gives me pause  and it makes me nervous and again i  don't think there's a planned hiatus i  have a hard time  understanding why that would make any  sense  but we might find ourselves  in a hiatus by default  because creators  are busy don't feel like  dealing with the fandom don't want to  play in this particular universe right  now  who knows but the longer the delay goes  on  the more it starts to feel like is there  nobody who's qualified who wants  the job  i don't know maybe hopefully not  like ultimately i hope that the first  thing i said is the reality that  they've got someone they just need to  lock stuff down and  finalize it or like they've got it down  to like two or three people and they're  just trying to sort out  exactly who whose schedule lines up best  or who had the best pitch or whatever  that's what i hope because and i always  say this whenever i talk about the  future of doctor who  i want this show to go on forever  there is never reasons to stop it there  is never a reason to reboot it  i would argue that at most maybe a  a breather of a little bit but there is  no reason to stop  the show is built to revitalize itself  and it can do that at a regular interval  and i will always always want the show  to continue  and i will always hope for the best for  it from the performers  from the writers the directors everyone  i love this show and even when i don't  like specific episodes or series or arcs  or creative decisions  i'm going to keep coming back because  i want it to be good and i want to enjoy  it  and it has yet to do anything for me  at least that has made me go i need to  walk away  is it impossible for it to do that no  but it hasn't happened yet and i don't  intend to  i love this show i wanted to keep going  and i want what's best for it  i just need to know who's steering this  ship  if anybody so there's my thoughts on the  delay in the current situation with the  lack of a newly announced showrunner for  doctor who  what are your thoughts on this be civil  please  to me to chibnall to anyone else who you  think might take this job  and even to other youtubers i know i  threw a little shade  a little bit but no personal attacks in  the comments i will delete your comment  and if it's bad enough  i'll just block you from being able to  comment just don't do it  don't be a jerk and i'll try not to be  but if you can keep it simple whatever  your thoughts are drop them down in the  comments let's talk about it  i have a patreon which is what pays my  bills enables me to do this  as my job any amount you're able to  support is a great help  don't worry about it though because like  share subscribe also helps me out a  great deal if you're not able to support  me financially  but even those things i'm not going to  pressure you too much because  at the end of the day you are the  council  i'm just running the meetings so until  next time this council  is adjourned  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  so  [Music]  um  [Music]
 

